{
  "id": "counting-house",
  "name": "The Counting House",
  "description": "Mother Rot's office on the top floor of a drowned bank in the Marsh. A long scarred table set for broth and business at once: a soup pot, cups, a closed paper ledger, brass scales, two green banker's lamps, and his patched leather chair at the head. Behind it three tall arched bank windows look across the canals to the Strand and the Wheel. On the left, a wall of old safe-deposit boxes used as shelving and a desk with an amber CRT and a telephone; on the right, an iron stove with a stockpot, a coat stand, and the service stairs going down to the water. Damp marble, peeling wallpaper, a dead chandelier, crates and rope on a warped parquet floor.",
